# The Mech Mayhem export fix — apply to the `robotworld` repo

This game's mechs come out of robotworld's `tools/export-mech.mjs`. Two defects
in that exporter are why a mech tore itself apart the moment it moved; the
diagnosis is written up under K15 in docs/mech-conversion-plan.md, and the
tools that found it are tools/probe_clip_coverage.mjs and
tools/verify_clip_fidelity.mjs in this repo.

This patch lives here because the two games are separate repositories and this
one is the one that ships the broken asset. Apply it upstream:

    cd <robotworld>
    git apply <mechbrawler>/docs/mm-export-fix.patch
    npx vite --port 5175 &
    node tools/export-mech.mjs --all --out public/models/export
    # then, in mechbrawler:
    python3 tools/fold_export.py <robotworld>/public/models/export/*.glb --apply

What it changes:

  * every clip is sampled for EVERY bone (`keep` was already passed for the
    held poses; actions and gaits pass it now), so a clip determines the whole
    skeleton instead of leaving the bones it does not move whereever the last
    one left them;
  * the sampler folds the root bone's yaw the same way `bakeModelTransform`
    folds the rest, for anyone who still wants a folded export; and
  * `?nofold` exports in the build's own frame, which is the mode this game
    uses — the transform then goes on the armature node (tools/fold_export.py)
    where it applies rigidly and cannot deform anything.

